  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 108 AM MDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will remain overhead on Monday resulting in \nanother day of mostly clear skies and seasonably mild temperatures. \nLight winds areawide. Upper level ridging shifts west to southern CA \nTuesday as a weak shortwave moves across the Colorado Rockies. This \nshortwave will result in a few light showers across the north \ncentral mountains near the CO border Tuesday afternoon. The \nshortwave moves south over the state Wednesday with it's axis \nhorizontally oriented from east to west. Daytime heating under the \nshortwave axis will result in a few isolated showers across the \nhigher terrain Wednesday afternoon. The upper high over the Great \nBasin Wednesday looks to move back over the Four Corners area and \ndesert SW Thursday breaking down Friday into next weekend with \ngenerally weak and variable flow overhead. In terms of the sensible \nweather, this will result in mostly clear skies and light winds. \nHigh temperatures will be in the low to mid 70s for lower elevations \nacross western and central NM and upper 70s to mid 80s across the \neastern plains during the long term period.",
